Size a hosted plugin's speaker arrangement from the speakers array's offset.

JUCE's VstSpeakerConfigurationHolder allocates
`(max(8, n) - 8) * sizeof (VstSpeakerProperties) + sizeof (VstSpeakerArrangement)`,
which is only right when the header declares `speakers[8]` as Steinberg's
original does, so that sizeof already covers eight. Plectrify compiles this
code against FST (a clean-room header, see CMakeLists.txt), which declares
`speakers[]` as a flexible array: sizeof is the two leading ints, the old
formula allocated 8 bytes for any arrangement of up to eight channels, and
the loop filling it wrote 112 bytes per speaker into the heap behind them.
The first real plugin loaded aborted in malloc a few calls later.

`offsetof (speakers) + max(8, n) * sizeof (VstSpeakerProperties)` is the same
number under either header.
diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTCommon.h b/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTCommon.h
index 84f409e5d..cbfe684e1 100644
--- a/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTCommon.h
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_processors_headless/format_types/juce_VSTCommon.h
@@ -227,8 +227,16 @@ struct SpeakerMappings  : private AudioChannelSet // (inheritance only to give e
 
         Vst2::VstSpeakerArrangement* allocate (int numChannels)
         {
-            auto arrangementSize = (size_t) (jmax (8, numChannels) - 8) * sizeof (Vst2::VstSpeakerProperties)
-                                    + sizeof (Vst2::VstSpeakerArrangement);
+            // PLECTRIFY_VST2_SPEAKER_ARRANGEMENT_SIZE: sized from the offset of the
+            // speakers array, not from sizeof (VstSpeakerArrangement). The original
+            // SDK header declares speakers[8], so sizeof already covers eight and
+            // the old formula added the rest; a header declaring a flexible array
+            // (FST does) has a sizeof of two ints, so that formula allocated 8
+            // bytes for any arrangement of up to eight channels, and the loop
+            // filling it then wrote 112 bytes per speaker into the heap behind
+            // them. This expression is the same number under either header.
+            auto arrangementSize = offsetof (Vst2::VstSpeakerArrangement, speakers)
+                                    + (size_t) jmax (8, numChannels) * sizeof (Vst2::VstSpeakerProperties);
 
             storage.malloc (1, arrangementSize);
             return storage.get();
